[
  {
    "sha": "e1fc569a9b47a12f25481835a6278c0b20d12f13",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGUxZmM1NjlhOWI0N2ExMmYyNTQ4MTgzNWE2Mjc4YzBiMjBkMTJmMTM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T00:41:48Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T00:41:48Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(turning): surface speed and feed per rev for lathe tools, G96 under a clamp\n\nLathe tools can state turning cutting data (Vc m/min, feed mm/rev, an\noptional max-rpm clamp). A turning table per work material (HSS and\ncarbide, conservative handbook-range values) feeds the \"Suggest feeds &\nspeeds\" of every turning op except threading: rpm at the stock's swing\ndiameter held to the tool's and machine's maxima, feed = f x rpm so the\nposted per-rev F is the table's. ApplyCuttingData writes op feed, plunge,\ntool rpm and turning data in one undo unit.\n\nThe stream carries PARAM SurfaceSpeed (+ MaxSpindleSpeed) for such ops;\nthe Fanuc lathe post writes G50 S<min clamp> + G96, Tormach G96 D<min>.\nA G96 with no clamp stated anywhere is refused by name in both posts.\nTools without turning data post unchanged (G97). The project file gains\nan additive `turning` key; old files load unchanged.\n\nFixes #891\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
