      "message": "feat(turning): a setup's workholding max rpm caps G96 and refuses G97 above it\n\nA lathe setup can state its chuck's or collet's rated maximum rpm\n(SetupDef::workholding_max_rpm, set by the undoable\nSetSetupWorkholdingRpm). Constant surface speed folds it into the\nsection's MaxSpindleSpeed ceiling, so Fanuc G50 S and Tormach G96 D post\nmin(machine, tool, workholding) with no post script change; a\nconstant-rpm turning op over it is refused by name at the program gate,\nthe setup named. The turning suggestion is held to it, a datum transfer\nkeeps it, and the project file gains an additive key.\n\nMCP tool set_workholding_max_rpm (get_job reports it); the Setups page\ngains a Workholding max rpm row, pinned in the structural twin.\n\nFixes #1031\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
